    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "After 22 years in our charming but cramped Waukesha brewery, we decided it was time to move and expand our exotic and classic car restoration mastery. Navigating cars around poles and up ramps had started to hinder our production. That led us in our search for a location that could handle our growing demand. We found our new home in Pewaukee, Wisconsin, in a spacious 35,000 sq. ft. building that previously housed a wood laminate production business. Although it needed significant renovations, we are always up for a restoration challenge!"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "With the help of our 20 dedicated employees, supportive friends, and a few outside specialists, we managed the move efficiently. Thanks to pre-moving a large portion of our inventory, we fully vacated our North St. location in just one week and resumed full production within a couple more weeks."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "images": [
        {
          "src": "../../assets/images/articles/FB-Banner-spooky.jpg",
          "alt": "",
          "caption": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "On June 4th, 2022, we celebrated our grand opening with an open house at the new facility. The excitement was palpable as we welcomed old, current, and prospective clients, along with many supportive friends."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "We’re thrilled about our new chapter in Pewaukee and look forward to serving our local and international clients for decades to come."
    },
